              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did vāḻttu mean, and what did mikka naṉṟi mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வாசல்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வாசல் (vāsal) — \"a doorway\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tamil separates the opening from the thing that shuts it. kadavu, which you have, is the door itself — the plank on its hinges. vāsal is the doorway: the gap, the step, and the strip of ground in front of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Almost everything that happens when a guest arrives happens at the vāsal rather than inside it, which is why the word carries more than architecture."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five things a guest meets at a Tamil door."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
