            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did vāsal mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கோலம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கோலம் (kōlam) — \"the design at a doorway\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Rice flour, drawn freehand on the ground each morning, usually by the woman of the house and usually before the sun is up. It is decoration and welcome at once — and because the flour feeds ants and birds, it is a small daily gift to whatever comes past."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The older sense of the word is 'form, appearance, the shape a thing takes'. A kōlam is the shape the house puts on to receive the day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: the doorway, and what is drawn in front of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
