          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: மலர்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மலர் (malar) — \"a flower\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The everyday word is pū, short and plain. malar is its fuller partner, the one that goes into names and poems and careful speech."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also says what a flower does: malar means 'to open, to blossom'. One shape names the act and the result of it, and Tamil saw no reason to invent a second word for the second thing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and the third one arrives in somebody's hand."
            }
          ]
        },
