        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வரவேற்பு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வரவேற்பு (varavēṟpu) — \"a welcome\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two pieces you can almost hear coming apart. vara is the coming, from vā, the word for 'come' you already have; ēṟpu is the accepting, from ēṟṟu, 'to receive'. A welcome, in Tamil, is the acceptance of somebody's arrival, and the word says that and nothing more."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "varavēṟkiṟēṉ is \"I welcome you\". At the vāsal, over the kōlam, with a malar and a veṟṟilai in hand, it is the last thing left to say at a door — and it sets you back down exactly where this book began, at a door, with vaṇakkam."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That closes the run: a doorway, a design, a flower, a leaf, and the word for taking somebody in."
            }
          ]
        },
